   CCoonntteexxtt LLoocckkiinngg
       When DRBGs are used by multiple threads, there must be locking employed
       to ensure their proper operation.  Because locking introduces an
       overhead, it is disabled by default.

       OOSSSSLL__FFUUNNCC__rraanndd__eennaabbllee__lloocckkiinngg(()) allows locking to be turned on for a
       DRBG and all of its parent DRBGs.  From this call onwards, the DRBG can
       be used in a thread safe manner.

       OOSSSSLL__FFUUNNCC__rraanndd__lloocckk(()) is used to lock a DRBG.  Once locked, exclusive
       access is guaranteed.

       OOSSSSLL__FFUUNNCC__rraanndd__uunnlloocckk(()) is used to unlock a DRBG.

